WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.187
- This is a story of when I realized

00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:03.734
why I don't date White guys.

00:00:05.945 --> 00:00:08.476
See, in the past it was
a long string of Latinos

00:00:08.476 --> 00:00:10.380
and a Korean and that didn't work out

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.702
and I'm missing out on
a whole dating pool.

00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:15.093
So I was like, "I'mma
open it up on ok cupid.

00:00:15.093 --> 00:00:16.523
"Let's date a White guy."

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.153
But I didn't figure out
my limits with White guys

00:00:19.153 --> 00:00:21.860
until my third date with this guy, Jim.

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:25.069
His real name wasn't Jim,

00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:26.718
but it was basically Jim.

00:00:26.718 --> 00:00:27.763
- My parents were totally right.

00:00:27.763 --> 00:00:30.036
The piano lessons really did pay off.

00:00:30.656 --> 00:00:31.989
- We're not gonna tell
them that though, right?

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:32.964
- No
(laughing)

00:00:32.964 --> 00:00:35.193
but I mean, me being a
professional musician

00:00:35.193 --> 00:00:36.447
might tip them off.

00:00:36.447 --> 00:00:38.560
- (laughing) Yeah, totally.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.789
During the walk, I could feel him

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:42.182
making a move,

00:00:42.182 --> 00:00:43.436
but I wasn't ready.

00:00:43.436 --> 00:00:45.316
So as he was leaning in,

00:00:45.316 --> 00:00:46.965
I blocked him, no!

00:00:46.965 --> 00:00:50.448
Hey, these plants aren't
native to California, right?

00:00:50.448 --> 00:00:52.955
- Hey, let's stop by my house.

00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:54.070
It's on the way to lunch.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.393
Let me show you those jazz records.

00:00:55.393 --> 00:00:56.299
- In his defense,

00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:58.853
we were actually talking
about his jazz records.

00:00:58.853 --> 00:01:00.943
Jim makes a beeline to his bedroom.

00:01:00.943 --> 00:01:03.125
As I follow him, I see something

00:01:03.125 --> 00:01:05.308
out of the corner of my eye.

00:01:05.308 --> 00:01:06.858
(menacing music)

00:01:07.839 --> 00:01:11.159
A set of decorative Samurai swords.

00:01:11.159 --> 00:01:14.108
And in that moment, a
rush of memories snap in.

00:01:14.108 --> 00:01:15.849
He did tell me on our first date

00:01:15.849 --> 00:01:17.614
that he taught English in Japan.

00:01:17.614 --> 00:01:20.075
And oh right, he did tell
me on our second date

00:01:20.075 --> 00:01:22.560
that he took Mandarin Chinese classes.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.487
What was I thinking?

00:01:24.487 --> 00:01:26.182
He wants to add me to his collection

00:01:26.182 --> 00:01:28.643
of decorative Oriental objects.

00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:31.035
You know, maybe it's just the one thing.

00:01:31.035 --> 00:01:32.381
What is it they say?

00:01:32.381 --> 00:01:33.844
Once is an accident.

00:01:33.844 --> 00:01:35.864
Twice is a coincidence.

00:01:35.864 --> 00:01:37.489
But three times?

00:01:37.489 --> 00:01:38.665
(menacing music)

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.551
Is an enemy action.

00:01:42.551 --> 00:01:45.964
I mean, even my extra Chinese
immigrant parent's house

00:01:45.964 --> 00:01:49.192
had three fewer calligraphy
scrolls than this guy.

00:01:49.192 --> 00:01:50.747
And in that moment of panic,

00:01:50.747 --> 00:01:53.093
I imagined that all Jim wanted was

00:01:53.093 --> 00:01:54.486
someone in that bedroom

00:01:54.486 --> 00:01:56.158
wearing a silky kimono robe,

00:01:56.158 --> 00:01:57.295
chopsticks in her hair

00:01:57.295 --> 00:01:58.990
and ribbon dancing for him.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:00.105
Because let's be honest,

00:02:00.105 --> 00:02:02.102
the only two sub-populations of people

00:02:02.102 --> 00:02:03.309
that I could possibly date

00:02:03.309 --> 00:02:04.215
who would have that many

00:02:04.215 --> 00:02:05.979
Chinese calligraphy scrolls on their walls

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:07.581
would be number one,

00:02:07.581 --> 00:02:10.089
real Asian gangster AZN
pride gangster dudes

00:02:10.089 --> 00:02:11.993
who have these scrolls, unironically,

00:02:11.993 --> 00:02:14.106
because that shit's beautiful.

00:02:14.106 --> 00:02:15.569
And the second group?

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:18.285
Owners of Chinatown curio gift shops

00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:19.725
who lack storage.

00:02:19.725 --> 00:02:21.280
I knew the day was over,

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.695
but I still wanted that Vietnamese food

00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:26.226
that Jim said was so good.

00:02:26.226 --> 00:02:27.596
I'm at the front door

00:02:27.596 --> 00:02:28.757
and as I'm putting on my shoes

00:02:28.757 --> 00:02:31.195
because, of course--

00:02:31.195 --> 00:02:32.565
Hey, what's that?

00:02:32.565 --> 00:02:34.004
- [Jim] Oh that's just the culmination

00:02:34.004 --> 00:02:35.839
of my entire music career.

00:02:35.839 --> 00:02:37.139
- In the middle of this plaque

00:02:37.139 --> 00:02:38.509
was a photo of him

00:02:38.509 --> 00:02:41.156
shaking the hand of an
old important White guy

00:02:41.156 --> 00:02:43.501
and Jim is wearing

00:02:43.501 --> 00:02:46.287
a blue silk China man jacket.

00:02:46.287 --> 00:02:49.074
For the biggest moment
of Jim's entire career,

00:02:49.074 --> 00:02:51.628
he wanted to look like Jackie Chan.

00:02:51.628 --> 00:02:52.464
That was it.

00:02:52.464 --> 00:02:54.604
I was like, I'm done with White land.

00:02:55.714 --> 00:02:57.990
I could see the bridge to White land

00:02:57.990 --> 00:03:00.404
and it looks really
great on the other side

00:03:00.404 --> 00:03:02.355
with their high cheek bones,

00:03:02.355 --> 00:03:04.770
J. Crew outfits and potato salad,

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.465
but I was done.

00:03:06.465 --> 00:03:08.160
First I thought, "You know what?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.040
"I'mma bomb this bridge to White land.

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.596
"No Jenny shall pass."

00:03:11.596 --> 00:03:13.012
And then I realized,

00:03:13.012 --> 00:03:15.172
it's not that I shouldn't
date any White guys,

00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:16.960
it's that I should not date a White guy

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.966
who's more Asian than me.

00:03:20.628 --> 00:03:22.039
(lively music)

